WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:06.650
It may be a faint dream, but let me see it
Hakanaki yume saredo yume misete

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:16.190
I'm in a complete daze under the sun
Konmei ryouran ni under the sun wow wow

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:20.920
Guided only by my flowering love for you
Konmei ryouran ni do ai do wow wow

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.530
Let the flower of life bloom
Hirakeyo inochi no hana

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:26.390
Let it follow its red hot desires
Akaku atsuku midasarete

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.550
This flame runs through the pulses
Fujouri na mirai no kodou

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.350
Of the absurd future
Kakenukeru honoo

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:36.450
I feel so guilty for devoting myself to earning your love
Aisaretakute kono mi sasageru tsumibukasa ga

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:40.570
I feel it tingling inside me
Watashi no naka de jirijiri shiteru ne

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.070
Desire
Yokubou

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:45.780
A bolt of lightning that brings about tomorrow
Sore wa ashita wo maneku inazuma

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:50.700
And turns into great pleasure
Yagate tsuyoi yorokobi ni naru

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:56.540
I'm sure you don't know yet
Mada shiranai hazu anata wa kitto

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.300
It's cruel when you can't even have a faint dream
Hakanaki yume saredo yume minu hibi wa mugoi yo

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:08.260
I want to hold on to these newborn desires
Umaretate no negai wo tada dakishimete itai

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:11.560
More wild than soft
Yasashii yori mo hageshiku ne

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.730
That will make my day
Sore de ima ga michite kuru sa

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:21.270
Who is going to protect this world (this dangerous world)
Michibikarete tashikameru sekai wa (ayaui sekai wa)

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.190
That I can only see for myself?
Dare ga mamoru

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:29.700
I can do it, so love me truly
Mamoreru dakara honki de ai shiteyo

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:31.490
<b>Graveyard</b>

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.910
What do you want?

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.500
Why did you revive us?

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:41.380
Answer me!

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.760
I know you can hear me!

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:47.930
You need not know.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.010
What?

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:53.730
You and Musashi should just get rid of the enemy.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:54.850
The enemy?

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:57.330
You mean the people at the Yagyuu dojo?

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:59.440
Anything and everything that lives.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.060
That means nothing to me!

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:05.530
Fool. Did you not see Mataemon's power?

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.530
Is that it?

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:09.360
What?

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:13.030
I believe you still need me.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.000
I just want to know.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.460
I want to know why I was revived.

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:21.500
<b>Yagyuu Dojo</b>

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.210
Why do I have to stay at home?

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.840
I cannot accept this!

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.750
There's nothing we can do.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:34.650
Yoshihiko-sama is at a location kept secret from us normal students.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.110
We should just wait for word from them.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.750
I'm a Master Samurai!

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:45.110
There was a time I offered my blood and sword to Yoshihiko-sama too!

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:46.790
Yet-

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:48.110
Where are you going?!

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:54.780
In my opinion, just staying up is a waste of time and energy.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:58.350
I'm going to go rest for a bit.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:01.070
H-Hey! Wait a minute!

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:03.170
I'm the leader here!

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:06.420
You can't just do whatever you want without the leader's permission!

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.590
If you're determined to oppose me,
you'll have to defeat-

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.510
Good night.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:17.750
Becoming a Master Samurai hasn't changed her at all.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.310
Indeed.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:20.810
<b>Underground Command Center</b>

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.400
<b>Yoshihiko</b>

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.990
Yoshihiko-sama, why did you summon us?

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:28.780
Sorry for calling you here like this,

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:35.430
but I'm sure you have a lot of questions for me right now.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:40.930
That's right, Onii-sama! First off, what is this Guardian Stone?

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:44.170
No one's telling me anything despite my persistence!

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:49.530
The Dark Samurai who attacked us were looking for the Guardian Stone!

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.260
I believe that gives us the right to know.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.910
You'd gain nothing from knowing.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.510
But if you insist.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:04.350
Imagine the Japanese archipelago is a human body. Qi flows through it like this.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:07.490
Japan's got qi too.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:12.990
Have you forgotten? Keiji said qi is in everything.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:15.410
I'm not suprised that the
archipelago is no exception.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:19.810
When the qi flows normally,
the country is stable.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:25.420
But if it's disturbed, the trinity of heaven, earth, and man will be disturbed as well.

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:28.910
Heaven, earth, and man?

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.670
Disturbance of heaven means chaotic weather.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.890
There will be typhoons and droughts.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.610
Disturbance of earth means the land itself.

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:37.230
There will be earthquakes
and volcanic eruptions.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:38.890
Disturbance of man means human chaos.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:41.210
There will be much more crime.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.310
I think that's the meaning.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:49.070
So to stabilize the flow of qi, a stone with great spiritual power was placed

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:53.570
under sacred Fuji, the focal point of the flow.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:54.500
<b>Guardian Stone</b>

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:54.530
That stone is the Guardian Stone.
<b>Guardian Stone</b>

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:55.820
<b>Guardian Stone
That stone is the Guardian Stone.</b>

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:59.080
No one knows who put the Guardian Stone there.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:03.080
Some speculate it was Queen Himiko or Prince Yamato Takeru.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.130
Could it be...

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:14.950
that the wars between clans on the archipelago calmed down, allowing the birth of Japan,

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:16.840
<i>because</i> the Guardian Stone was put in place?

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:22.220
Here, Great Japan is beautiful.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:27.150
However, there are some who work against peace.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:32.770
There are people who have damaged the Guardian Stone in the past.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:36.530
Every time, Great Japan was
engulfed in war and conflict.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.870
The greatest of those was Amakusa Shirou.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:45.630
She targeted the Guardian Stone numerous times to cause such catastrophes.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:52.590
Most recently during the World War,
Japan was on the brink of destruction.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:53.510
And at that time...

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:57.690
Rin! Pyo! To! Sha! Kai! Jin! Retsu! Zai! Zen!

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:58.630
What is that?

00:05:58.630 --> 00:05:59.170
Rin! Pyo! To! Sha! Kai! Jin! Retsu! Zai! Zen!

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:00.340
A barrier spell.

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:01.390
Rin! Pyo! To! Sha! Kai! Jin! Retsu! Zai! Zen!

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:06.850
The Tokugawa shogunate decided to protect the Guardian Stone and reinforce the barriers.

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:08.690
Barriers?
Rin! Pyo! To! Sha! Kai! Jin! Retsu! Zai! Zen!

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:12.930
Dozens of barriers are focused around the Guardian Stone.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:16.360
The center of those is here, at Buou Academy.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:18.990
So the Academy is a part of the barrier too?

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:26.120
The barrier won't allow anyone with evil intent to disrupt the peace near the Guardian Stone.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:29.650
As long as the barriers are intact, the Guardian Stone is stable.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.750
With it, the world of the Tokugawa as well.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:33.590
At least, that was the intent.

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:38.590
But they're chanting a spell to repair the barrier.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:42.870
Does that mean the barrier needs repairs?

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:45.090
That's a grave situation!

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:47.140
You say that as if it wasn't directly related to you.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:49.890
Yes, this situation has
everything to do with you.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:55.440
Was it during my fight with Gittan?

00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:00.700
While Amakusa is our enemy,
I must admit she played her hand well.

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:06.120
They infiltrated the Academy while purified so that the barriers wouldn't react to them

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.950
and tried to complete their return while inside.

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:10.920
While they failed,

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:17.390
the great battle inside the barrier damaged it severely.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:21.800
I see! So the barriers were weakened.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:23.290
As a result,

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:27.810
some evil spirits that harbored enmity against the Tokugawa shogunate were able to revive.

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:31.270
We can't accept the peace of the Tokugawa.

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:34.510
Samurai are meant to die in battle.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:37.650
War is what we truly desire.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:42.510
The spirits have tried a number of ways.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:44.280
They tried possessing people and animals.

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:47.850
One time, they even reanimated a hundred dead bodies at once.

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:49.700
I never knew about that.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:56.340
Because Nia and my Master Samurai fought valiantly to thwart their plans.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:58.000
Thank you, Nia-san.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:05.070
But a month ago, they made a powerful move.

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:07.850
They revived four incredibly powerful samurai.

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:09.750
The Dark Samurai!

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:12.690
They want to use them to get us out of the way.

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:21.150
The four of you were revived to get rid of Tokugawa Yoshihiko's Master Samurai.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:25.270
Defeat the Master Samurai, destroy the Guardian Stone,

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.990
and turn Tokugawa's peace into an era of chaos!

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:30.790
Th-That was it?

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.590
We were defeated.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:36.270
We didn't stand a chance.

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:56.650
Not bad. They don't call you the strongest Master Samurai for nothing.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:59.650
But in a dual-wielding battle...

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:04.410
I'm the strongest.

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:08.430
No.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:13.350
I'm not the strongest Master Samurai.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:14.870
The fuck are you joking about?

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:18.830
We know you defeated Amakusa Shirou!

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:20.550
<i>I</i> didn't defeat her.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:26.340
It was Yagyuu Muneakira and his Master Samurai.

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:31.560
The strongest among them is the dual-wielder Yagyuu Juubei.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:35.470
The Yagyuu dojo... Yagyuu Juubei...

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.520
That was my order.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:43.820
"Say Yagyuu Juubei's name if your life is in danger."

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:47.730
That's why they came to the Yagyuu dojo?

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.700
So we were the last line of defense?

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:54.170
I just wanted you to buy us some time.

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:59.210
I didn't think Juubei could become a Master Samurai anymore.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:01.960
We bought you time.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:05.590
You succeeded purely through luck.

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:11.970
It was our mistake to not tell you anything so you could focus solely on fighting.

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:17.250
Musashi got so obsessed with fighting Yagyuu Juubei,

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.060
she gave them an entire month's time.

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:24.750
But in that month, they were able to repair the barriers.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:29.450
So we used Mataemon to look for the Guardian Stone.

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:32.410
Why Mataemon?

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:34.910
Just look at her.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:44.840
It must be because of what she did in life.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:49.590
Her body wasn't revived in perfect condition.

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:52.510
We completed her as a puppet.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.870
Only a small part of her is organic,

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:59.440
so she's far easier for us to manipulate than you or Musashi.

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:03.000
We couldn't ask for a better puppet.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:05.770
So she really <i>is</i> just a marionette now, huh?

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.440
Wait, then what about Inshun?

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:11.490
She seemed to be aware of what's going on.

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:12.990
She's a spirit vessel.

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:14.610
A spirit vessel?

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:16.510
When the time comes, you'll know.

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:19.000
Revenge! Revenge!

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:21.620
Kill! Kill!

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:24.210
Help me. Help me!
I want to slash them!

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:31.430
I wish you could buy us one more day, though.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:34.870
What do you mean, Onii-sama?

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:41.610
The repairs to the barrier will be completed the day after your match with the Dark Samurai.

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:44.530
Couldn't we postpone the match?

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:49.280
No, they'd take notice if we did that, and they'd break our agreement.

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:52.390
As long as they don't see us pulling any stunts,

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:56.610
Miyamoto Musashi at least will give priority to the match.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:58.540
Inko-chan too!

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:01.130
I know Inko-chan will keep her promise!

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:04.070
She's not the type of person to destroy Japan.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:07.880
We promised to become friends after the match!

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.800
What should we do, then?

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:13.010
Proceed according to the schedule.

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:15.680
Fight the Dark Samurai and win.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:18.970
That's easier said than done.

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:22.370
The barriers will be completely repaired the day after tomorrow,

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:24.930
and the vengeful spirits will be immobilized.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:32.190
They won't be able to grant powers to the defeated Dark Samurai again or revive new ones.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:36.530
If you wish for our victory,
then we have one condition.

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:39.210
The documents on the Samurai Bride, I assume?

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:43.430
Sen's documents were missing critical sections.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:45.170
They must be somewhere.

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:48.510
Although I doubt a legend like that would help,

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:49.960
if that's what you want, then...

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:56.830
I'll have all books in the Tokugawa secret archives that relate to the Samurai Bride delivered to you.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:59.100
Thank you very much, Yoshihiko-sama.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:03.590
Give it your best. I'm hoping for another pleasant surprise,

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:05.440
Yagyuu Muneakira.

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:07.440
<b>The Next Morning</b>

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.110
<b>Graveyard</b>

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:15.320
You came back?

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:19.470
Where's Inshun?

00:13:21.140 --> 00:13:22.160
Where's Mataemon?

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:25.620
Mataemon is...

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:26.710
What's wrong?

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:32.380
They don't matter, do they?

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:37.970
Mataemon?!

00:13:39.890 --> 00:13:41.230
Mataemon?

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:44.790
I heard everything.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:45.830
Everything?

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.580
The stuff about your body too?

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.110
Yeah.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.490
Hilarious!

00:13:54.490 --> 00:13:56.210
You don't mind it?

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:57.070
Mind what?

00:13:57.070 --> 00:13:59.170
What happened to your body.

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:00.390
What?

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:03.210
This body is so much fun.

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:05.390
There's nothing to complain about!

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:07.620
Or are you jealous?

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:09.830
Don't be ridiculous!

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:11.190
Now, then.

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:14.970
Where are you going?

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:18.250
To search for the Guardian Stone, of course.

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.130
That's what I'm here for, you know?

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:22.990
But you won't find anybody on the streets at this hour.

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:24.770
I'm not talking about attacking people.

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:26.850
What? But...

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:29.770
I have a good idea of where it is.

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:32.190
I read the memory of that Sen girl, after all.

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:34.230
Oh, I see.

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:36.230
Wanna tag along?

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:38.860
You don't have to go with Musashi,
who's only obsessed with that match.

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:41.910
B-But I...

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:47.210
Seriously?!

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:48.510
That's so hilarious!

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:53.390
I like the action genre more than I do romance!

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:55.530
Give my regards to that combat freak!

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.760
They <i>do</i> matter.

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.410
So where did...

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:01.950
No idea.

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.800
At any rate...

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:09.730
Which do you prefer, the world as it is now now or the world during war?

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:10.850
What kind of question is that?

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:11.940
Answer me!

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:16.820
All I want is to fight strong people.

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:18.860
I want to fight Yagyuu Juubei.

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:21.910
You really are a combat freak.

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:26.390
I'm a samurai too.

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:29.000
I want to fight strong people,

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:31.810
but when a war breaks out,

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:35.330
I won't be able to tell who are my enemies or who my allies.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:36.920
Musashi could be...

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:39.300
Kojirou!

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:43.930
At any rate, we have a match with the Yagyuu dojo in two days.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:45.790
Don't forget.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.290
I know.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:48.390
And...

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:51.710
If you see Mataemon,

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:55.650
tell her I'm gonna beat the crap out of her for being so inhuman.

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:02.190
Right. Mataemon is indeed not human.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:04.360
<b>Sanada Style</b>

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:07.240
<b>Speed Reading Technique</b>

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:14.960
Is she even reading?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.190
Sanada-style speed reading technique.

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:21.220
It's a way of reading where only the essential words are recognized and registered.

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:25.090
It's useful when there's limited time.

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:27.450
But it's Yukimura.

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:30.350
Even if she finds the conditions for becoming a Samurai Bride,

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:32.730
she probably won't tell us.

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:34.270
You should trust her more.

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.130
Don't worry.

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:37.390
Even if that's the case,

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.940
love will prevail in the end!

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:43.810
The warrior of love will become the Samurai Bride!

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:46.110
That's me, Naoe Kanetsugu!

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:49.530
What is it?!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.500
Got a problem with that?

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:57.290
But if it's something even Kanetsugu-san can become, then I have a chance too!

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.340
Hanzou-san!

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:02.550
You're the right person to be my Samurai Bride!

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:05.590
But what about the princess?

00:17:05.590 --> 00:17:07.470
You're all my eyes can see.

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:11.250
I'm so sorry, milady!

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:14.550
I've become his Samurai Bride!

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:16.770
Who's the Samurai Bride?

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:17.650
No, um...

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:20.510
So you're after it too!

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.310
You've got it all wrong!

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:26.910
The Samurai Bride, huh?

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:28.390
I wonder who it'll be.

00:17:28.390 --> 00:17:31.740
Onee-sama, don't you want to be it yourself?

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:33.790
I'm not denying my interest, but...

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:34.620
But?

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:39.130
You have to fight a lot when you
become a Samurai Bride, don't you?

00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:46.260
I'll have to fight with Mucchan, Inko-chan, and a bunch of other people too.

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:48.330
I don't want to do that.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.510
I want to become friends with everyone.

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:53.790
What's the matter, Gittan?

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:56.140
That just irritated me a little.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:18:01.270
You seem to assume that you can win easily when you're a Samurai Bride.

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:04.010
Onee-sama, you're mine.

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:07.070
Nobody else should be able to defeat you.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.370
Please keep that in mind.

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:15.750
Just a bit longer.

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:19.470
No matter what happens, I need to be ready in two days.

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:22.000
<b>Yagyuu Dojo</b>

00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:24.760
<b>Yagyuu Muneakira</b>

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:31.430
Damn! I really can't do it.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:34.560
Even though we only have two days left!

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:46.280
Rin! Pyo! To! Sha! Kai! Jin! Retsu! Zai!

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:28.190
What?

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:29.990
I see.

00:19:29.990 --> 00:19:34.430
This is why a General can only have one Samurai Bride.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:36.830
Matabei!

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:38.410
At your service.

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:40.110
Gather the others.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:43.540
I've learned the secret of the Samurai Brides!

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:49.290
We made it just in time.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.510
I'm prepared.

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:54.550
Probably only I will fit the requirements.

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:58.060
I'll have beast Muneakira all for myse-

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:02.190
Yukimura, go on.

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:06.190
I read and analyzed all the documents.

00:20:06.190 --> 00:20:11.820
It's clear that there are multiple conditions for the birth of a Samurai Bride.

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:14.160
Multiple conditions?

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:16.950
Yes. Judging from prior cases,

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:22.160
the General must have at least seven Master Samurai bound to him.

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:29.430
Milady, Yukimura-san, Juubei-san, Kanetsugu-san, Matabei-san, and me.

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:31.610
Oh my! We're only six!

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:34.680
I stand corrected. Seven.

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:42.390
All seven Master Samurai must have strong emotional ties focusing around one of them.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:44.330
Strong ties...

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:51.780
And lastly, the other Master Samurai must give that one all of their qi.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.950
All of it?

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:57.700
And it must pass through the General.

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:03.670
What happens if someone pours out all her qi?

00:21:03.670 --> 00:21:07.410
What happens if someone takes in all the qi of seven others?

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:09.090
I think we all know.

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:13.050
The other Master Samurai will probably lose all their power,

00:21:13.050 --> 00:21:15.210
and the General's life will also be in danger.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:18.260
There were cases in the past where all of them died.

00:21:22.430 --> 00:21:23.980
No way!

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:30.770
All the others die when a Samurai Bride is born?

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:32.490
That can't be!

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:36.740
Episode Ten

00:23:10.850 --> 00:23:13.990
All 130 million Tokugawa fans around the nation!

00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:17.030
I am the great hero, Tokugawa Yoshihiko!

00:23:17.720 --> 00:23:19.370
The cameraman is already here.

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:21.850
Be sure to film my heroic actions again.

00:23:21.850 --> 00:23:25.230
Nia! You're gonna appear too, so fix your makeup!

00:23:25.230 --> 00:23:27.770
My General, please refrain from taking pictures of me.

00:23:27.770 --> 00:23:29.710
You don't like people taking photos of you?

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:31.690
It feels like someone's trying to steal my soul. It's unsettling.

00:23:31.690 --> 00:23:32.980
I-I see.

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:35.510
Next time: The Showdown

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:39.990
And sometimes strange shadows show up in the background.
